                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I loved the flash game where you had to demolish buildings with UFO, so I happily got this super cheap game, expected some fun hours, but this game ends up as very disappointing:\n\n+Super cheap on sale, game price nearly covered by steam cards\n+Steam achievements\n-Called airstrike *HD*, expected the game to look good - instead it looks horrible + Menu HUD gives away obvious port from mobile phones ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯ static background drawn by 7 years old, useless crowd that you can't damage at all looks bad as well, cartoonish buildings while planes pretend to be noncartoonish, so overall the visual side of the game is horrible.\n\n-Sound - lame music + bad sound work, nothing more to say\n\n-Gameplay - horrible controls, because bomb drops totally unreliable, maybe because this game is made on unity (most likely), you can't trust your bombs when you are dropping them from a high height, and it always results in losing the game. \n\n-Rеtаrded bonus system, you have bonus boxes which you can bomb OR ignore, most of the bonuses are BAD for you, picking up bad bonus is 90% loss of the game, and if you don't pick up the bonus you can't bomb the building under this bonus, so you may lose the round as well. This is just BAD. So when you are done with this sh`t you have an option to turn on in-game HAX, which turns the table to a completely opposite situation when the game is boring to the limit.\n\nTl;DR - the game has only 2 states - frustrating or boring af",
